{
  "_comment": [
    "ECX CLOBBERERS -- __watcall-family functions that do NOT preserve ECX, and therefore must stay",
    "on __mh_watcall_ecx_volatile now that __watcall itself declares ECX <unaffected>.",
    "",
    "GENERATED: run mh_classify_reg_preservation.py in Ghidra, then",
    "`python tools/gen_reg_clobberers.py`. Applied by mh_set_calling_convention.py. Do not",
    "hand-edit. A function that becomes a clobberer and is NOT on this list gets a silently stale",
    "ECX at every call site, which reads as correct code -- the failure this whole split exists to",
    "prevent.",
    "",
    "`why` records which test caught it: `clobbers` writes ECX with no covering PUSH; `unsure`",
    "pushes it but no exit path was proven to restore it (treated as a clobberer deliberately, since",
    "the conservative error costs only an honest artifact).",
    "",
    "Functions on __stdcall / __cdecl / __mhfastocall are EXCLUDED by construction: those models kill",
    "ECX already, and forcing a __watcall-derived model onto them would change parameter passing."
  ],
